    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. so you're saying it's basically a necessity for the climate then? i've heard some people say it's just an unfair tax on people who can't afford to live closer to work or those who have to drive for their jobs. if it's so \"non-optional,\" how do planners address the fact that it seems to punish the working class more than the wealthy?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
